# qforge: enable the SSH server on release. It ships ON now, not gated by any switch — remote
# access is key-only (no password on any account, no baked key), so a running sshd with no
# authorized key admits nobody. Keys arrive through the key-delivery daemon (qforge-pairingd),
# which is always on for now. /etc/machine-id is empty on a fresh image so systemd
# runs preset-all on first boot, where the stock 99-default.preset is "disable *"; this
# higher-priority preset (60 < 99) keeps sshd enabled. A build-time multi-user.target.wants
# symlink ships alongside as a fallback (cf. 60-qforge-powerd). Host keys are generated
# per-device at first start by openssh's own sshdgenkeys.service, not baked here.
enable sshd.service
